"""Results Reporting Script for modelC

Purpose: Generate comprehensive results report from modelC predictions:
         - Metrics table (CSV + LaTeX)
         - Precision-Recall curve (PNG + PDF) with baseline prevalence
         - Risk map showing Colombia boundary, top-1% predicted pixels, and observed PA establishments
         - Probability map showing continuous probability predictions across Colombia

Input:   - modelC_{model_type}_win5_metrics_*.json
         - modelC_{model_type}_win5_scored_*.parquet (raw or calibrated)
         - test_colombia_win5.parquet (optional, auto-discovered if available)

Supports model types: lgbm, rf, brf

Note:    The risk map uses WDPA_b1 from original test data to correctly identify pixels
         established in each year. Since transition_01_win5 (y_true) is a 5-year lookahead
         target, it doesn't mark the actual year of establishment. For example, pixels
         established in 2018 have y_true=1 only for years before 2018, not for 2018 itself.
         By loading WDPA_b1 from the original test data, we ensure all establishments
         are correctly shown.

Output:  - outputs/Results/results_modelC_{model_type}/
           - modelC_{model_type}_metrics_table.csv
           - modelC_{model_type}_metrics_table.tex
           - modelC_{model_type}_pr_curve.png
           - modelC_{model_type}_pr_curve.pdf
           - modelC_{model_type}_risk_map_top1pct.png
           - modelC_{model_type}_risk_map_top1pct.pdf
           - modelC_{model_type}_probability_map.png
           - modelC_{model_type}_probability_map.pdf
"""

